Adapted files:

  lib/src/voice_profile_matching.dart
    from packages/cc_domain/lib/features/meetings/domain/services/
    voice_profile_matching.dart
    The matching, blending and un-blending math is unchanged. The functions now
    take SpeakerEmbedding instead of List<double>, so a comparison across two
    embedding spaces returns null rather than a plausible number; the 0.70 /
    0.50 thresholds moved out of the algorithm into a caller-supplied
    VoiceMatchThresholds carrying its own provenance; blendCentroid no longer
    falls back to a fresh start on a space mismatch; and the per-profile
    Float32List.fromList allocation is gone because the vector is stored once.
    The cosine-similarity kernel it calls (lib/src/embedding.dart,
    speakerSimilarity) is adapted from
    packages/cc_domain/lib/core/domain/services/cosine_similarity.dart, with
    the length check replaced by an embedding-space check and the result
    clamped to the cosine range.

Portions of the accompanying test suite are likewise adapted from Control
Center's test/features/meetings/voice_profile_matching_test.dart.
